t rebuild series of the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) spanning 2026-09-26 to 2026-10-01, covering commits b10146 \u2192 b12321. Context A (Claude Opus 5.5) ran 09-26 to 09-28 on an i915 driver; Context B (Claude Sonnet 5.5) resumed 10-01 after the A770 switched to the `xe` driver by other sessions.\n\n- **Host setup:** Built on `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 9 7900X3D, 64 GB DDR5, Intel Arc A770 16 GB headless GPU) running Arch Linux with mergerfs at `/mnt/mrgr`; elevated commands via `ssh -o BatchMode=yes`.\n\n- **Major technical work:** Included a PKGBUILD rework, debugging a `LLAMA_SUBPROCESS` ABI trap (commit d37dd50bb), SYCL graphs, oneDNN A/B testing, a oneAPI 2026.0 \u2192 2026.1 swap (DLE swap), PR #63 benchmark review, an IGC crash fixed with a DG2 XMX-gather patch (commit 4e7400c3a), 256-GRF kernels, and a 12-vs-18 t/s decode investigation.\n\n- **Deliverables:** Produced a complete session record with 15 chronological phases, technical analyses, consolidated benchmark tables,"}